-- חוק הפרשנות, התשמ"א-1981 — sections 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 10: what the
-- law applies to; that a defined term carries its definition; that a
-- person includes a body of persons, the singular the plural and the male
-- the female; that "or" and "other" add to a list rather than liken to it;
-- that "עד" in a matter of time or of a quoted passage includes its bound;
-- and how a period is counted. The text is laws/interpretation-law.toml,
-- pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy
-- (MMS-689).
--
-- Why these: §25(ד) of the Contracts Law applies sections 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8
-- and 10 to reading a contract (l4/laws/contracts-law.l4), and that is the
-- route by which they reach a collective agreement — the law itself, by
-- §1, speaks of an enactment and an administrative instruction. How they
-- reach the circulars and the takanon is the convention
-- reading.interpretation-law, a pick for the lawyer.
--
-- Each section applies "if no other provision governs the matter and
-- nothing in the matter or its context is inconsistent with it" (§1, §2;
-- §25(ד) of the Contracts Law says the same of a contract). That proviso
-- is an input to every rule here, never assumed away.

IMPORT prelude

§ `חוק הפרשנות — פירוש מלים, ביטויים ותקופות`

§§ `1`

-- The law applies to every enactment and administrative instruction, even
-- one given before it, where no other provision governs the matter and
-- nothing in it or its context is inconsistent; §3's definitions do not
-- reach words in an enactment or instruction given before it (save "חטא",
-- "עוון" and "פשע"), which keep the Interpretation Ordinance's §1.
-- "Administrative instruction" (§3): an instruction or appointment, a
-- notice, a licence, a permit and the like, given in writing under a law
-- and not legislative.
@desc An instrument, as the Interpretation Law and the Contracts Law bring this law to it.
DECLARE `instrument the Interpretation Law meets` IS ONE OF
    `an enactment, as the Interpretation Law counts it`
    `an administrative instruction given in writing under a law`
    `a contract, as the Interpretation Law meets it`
    `an instrument that is neither`

@desc How the Interpretation Law reaches an instrument.
DECLARE `how the Interpretation Law reaches it` IS ONE OF
    `every section, under section 1`
    `sections 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 10, under section 25(ד) of the Contracts Law`
    `not by its own force`

@ref law:1
GIVEN i IS AN `instrument the Interpretation Law meets`
GIVETH A `how the Interpretation Law reaches it`
DECIDE `how the Interpretation Law reaches the instrument` i IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `an enactment, as the Interpretation Law counts it` THEN `every section, under section 1`
    WHEN `an administrative instruction given in writing under a law` THEN `every section, under section 1`
    WHEN `a contract, as the Interpretation Law meets it` THEN `sections 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 10, under section 25(ד) of the Contracts Law`
    OTHERWISE `not by its own force`

@ref law:1
GIVEN `another provision governs the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Interpretation Law applies to the matter` `another provision governs the matter` `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it` IF
        NOT `another provision governs the matter`
    AND NOT `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it`

§§ `2`

-- A term an enactment defines carries its definition, in regulations under
-- it too, and in every grammatical form derived from it — unless another
-- provision governs the matter or the context is inconsistent.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `another provision governs the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a defined term carries its definition under section 2` `another provision governs the matter` `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it` IF
    `the Interpretation Law applies to the matter` `another provision governs the matter` `the matter or its context is inconsistent with it`

§§ `4`

-- Where a person is spoken of, a body of persons is meant too, incorporated
-- or not.
@ref law:4
`a body of persons is a person under section 4` MEANS TRUE

§§ `5`

-- The singular includes the plural, and the plural the singular.
@ref law:5
`the singular includes the plural under section 5` MEANS TRUE

§§ `6`

-- The male includes the female, and the female the male: a provision of
-- an agreement written in one gender ("על שם אשתו") speaks to both
-- (convention instruments.equal-pay-teaching reads it so).
@ref law:6
`the male includes the female under section 6` MEANS TRUE

§§ `7`

-- "Or", "other" and the like add to the items listed before them and are
-- not likened to them, unless "similar", "the like" or another word of
-- likeness stands with them.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `a word of likeness stands with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `"or" or "other" is likened to the items before it under section 7` `a word of likeness stands with it` IS
    `a word of likeness stands with it`

§§ `8`

-- "עד…" in a matter of time or of a quoted passage means up to and
-- including. The section says nothing of an amount, a rate or a count:
-- there it is silent, and the encoding's convention thresholds.until reads
-- "עד N" (whether an age is a matter of time is the question MMS-689
-- puts to the client).
@ref law:8
GIVEN `it is a matter of time or of a quoted passage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8 includes the bound "עד" names` `it is a matter of time or of a quoted passage` IS
    `it is a matter of time or of a quoted passage`

@ref law:8
GIVEN `the value` IS A NUMBER, `the bound "עד" names` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the value is within "עד" the bound under section 8` `the value` `the bound "עד" names` IF
    `the value` AT MOST `the bound "עד" names`

§§ `10`

-- (א): a period of so many days or weeks from a given day does not count
-- that day, so it ends on the day that many days after it. Days here are
-- day numbers on one count.
@ref law:10
GIVEN `the given day` IS A NUMBER, `days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last day of a period of days from a day under section 10(א)` `the given day` `days in the period` IS
    `the given day` PLUS `days in the period`

-- (ב): a period of so many months or years after an event ends, in its last
-- month, on the day of that month numbered as the event's day; where that
-- month has no such day, on its last day.
@ref law:10
GIVEN `the event's day of the month` IS A NUMBER, `days in the period's last month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day of the last month a period of months ends on under section 10(ב)` `the event's day of the month` `days in the period's last month` IS
    IF `the event's day of the month` AT MOST `days in the period's last month`
    THEN `the event's day of the month`
    ELSE `days in the period's last month`

-- (ג): days of rest, recess or holiday set by an enactment count in the
-- days of a period, unless they are its last days.
@ref law:10
GIVEN `the day is among the period's last days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a day of rest counts in the period under section 10(ג)` `the day is among the period's last days` IF
    NOT `the day is among the period's last days`
